ssembly at $E668-$E678 is the debounce+store: it stores the merged value to $FA,X. X=0 → $FA. Yes.\n\nActually wait, let me re-examine. $E66C sta $F8,X stores merged to $F8. Then PHA, EOR $FA,X, AND $F8,X, STA $F8,X → $F8 = edge. PLA, STA $FA,X → $FA = merged current. So yes, after the routine: $F8 = newly pressed (edge), $FA = current held. For X=1: $F9 edge, $FB current.\n\nGood. Now let's also verify the pause flag with a write proof: write 0x00E0 = 1 while playing and confirm the game freezes (Link won't move). Let me do that.\n\nCurrently, is the game paused? After the button script, Start was pressed which opens the item subscreen, then released. The subscreen might be open (game_mode 8). Hmm, Start opens subscreen and it stays open until Start again. My script pressed Start for 12 frames then released → subscreen opened and stayed open. Then 20 frames idle. So now the item subscreen is displayed. Let me reload the save state for a clean start before further tests.\n\nLet me: load_state file again (clean overworld), verify screenshot, then write 0x00E0=1 and hold Right, check Link frozen; then write 0x00E0=0 to resume and check Link moves.\n\nActually write proof for pause: while playing, write 0x00E0=1. Does the game freeze? The flag may be checked by the main loop; writing it should halt movement. Let's test.\n\nPlan:\n1. load_state clean.\n2. read 0x0070 and 0x00E0.\n3. write 0x00E0 = 1.\n4. play_input hold right 40, watch 0x0070, 0x00E0.\n5. If Link frozen → proof. Then write 0x00E0=0 and hold right to confirm he moves again.\n\nLet me do it. Note: after write, the game might reset it each frame (it's live RAM). If the game's main loop only sets 0x00E0 on Select, writing 1 should persist. Let's try."}
